        Donald E. Knuth defined the TRIP\ test\ to validate his second
implementation of \TeX\ in 1982. It is still an important part of
his \TeX\ distribution as it must nowadays be used to validate a
concrete implementation. This article does not describe the contents
of this test in detail. It concentrates on the history and the impact
of the TRIP\ test. The text explains why this test was generated, discusses
the test's successes and failures, and relates the test to the
state of software testing at the time of its creation.
